If you know a better way just ping me and I can try to make it happen.
Also if you want to somehow make the official package list available to the ci, I think it would have to be moved to a separate package.

I checked all `Cargo.toml` files that are shipped with `bevy_macro_utils` but they don't contain a list of all official bevy packages.

Would you be interested in a `bevy_build_info` package that contains the following kind of information?

<details>

<summary>Sample code for exposing environment and build information to bevy users</summary>

```rust
/// This is information about the bevy build and the user build.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Eq, PartialEq, Hash, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct BuildInfo {
  // Version information
  pub cargo_pkg_version: Semver,
  pub git_version: String,
  pub git_submodule_versions: Vec<(String, String)>,

  // Build information
  pub build_date: DateTime<Utc>,
  pub library_linking_type: LibraryLinkingType,
  pub enabled_features: Vec<String>,
  pub overflow_checks: bool,
  pub panic_strategy: String,
  pub relocation_model: String,

  // Target information
  pub target_os: String,
  pub target_family: String,
  pub target_arch: String,
  pub target_features: Vec<String>,
  pub target_pointer_width: usize,
  pub target_endianness: Endianness,
  pub target_env: String,
  // Target information less relevant
  pub target_has_atomic: Vec<String>,
  pub target_has_atomic_equal_alignment: Vec<String>,
  pub target_has_atomic_load_store: Vec<String>,

  // Compiler information
  pub rustc_version: String,
  pub rustup_toolchain: String,
  pub target_triple: String,
  pub host_triple: String,
  pub opt_level: String,
  pub debug: bool,
  pub profile: String,
  pub rustflags: Vec<String>,
  // Linker information
  pub linker: String,
  pub clang_version: String,
  pub lld_version: String,
  pub ld_version: String,
  pub mold_version: String,
}

/// This is information about the machine that is running bevy
pub struct GPUInformation {
  pub model: String,
  pub vendor: String,
  pub memory_total: usize,
  pub memory_used: usize,
  pub memory_available: usize,
}

/// This is information about the machine that is running bevy
pub struct MachineInformation {
  // OS Information
  pub os_name: String,
  pub os_version: String,
  pub kernel_version: String,
  pub current_working_directory: PathBuf,
  pub executable_path: PathBuf,
  /// Time since the machine booted
  pub machine_uptime: Duration,

  // CPU Information
  pub cpu_count: usize,
  pub cpu_model: String,
  pub cpu_vendor: String,
  /// The frequency of the CPU in MHz.
  pub cpu_frequency: Option<f64>,
  /// L1, L2, L3 in KB
  pub cpu_cache_sizes: BTreeMap<String, usize>,

  // GPU Information
  pub gpu_information: Vec<GPUInformation>,

  // IO Information
  /// The amount of installed memory in bytes.
  pub memory_total: usize,
  /// The amount of used memory in bytes.
  pub memory_used: usize,
  /// The amount of free memory in bytes.
  pub memory_free: usize,

  /// The amount of total SWAP in bytes.
  pub swap_total: usize,
  /// The amount of used SWAP in bytes.
  pub swap_used: usize,
  /// The amount of free SWAP in bytes.
  pub swap_free: usize,

  /// The total disk space in bytes of the drive where the executable is located.
  pub disk_usage_total: usize,
  /// The used disk space in bytes of the drive where the executable is located.
  pub disk_usage_used: usize,
  /// The free disk space in bytes of the drive where the executable is located.
  pub disk_usage_free: usize,

  pub active_network_interfaces: Vec<String>,

  // Important Environment Variables
  pub rust_log: Option<String>,
  pub rust_backtrace: Option<String>,
  pub path: String,

  // Environment Variables Library Loading
  pub ld_preload: Option<String>,
  pub ld_library_path: Option<String>,
  pub dyld_library_path: Option<String>,

  // Environment Variables Proxy
  pub http_proxy: Option<String>,
  pub https_proxy: Option<String>,
  pub no_proxy: Option<String>,

  // Environment Variables Locale
  pub lang: Option<String>,
  pub lc_all: Option<String>,
  pub lc_messages: Option<String>,

  // Environment Variables Timezone
  pub tz: Option<String>,
  pub tzdata: Option<String>,
  pub tzdir: Option<String>,

  // Environment Variables remaining
  pub environment_variables: BTreeMap<String, String>,
}
```

The above is unrefined and just here to give you an idea of what I did for my own project.


</details>
